  "id": "Compound::DB01242 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Clomipramine is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a series of interconnected pathways involving the enzyme cytochrome P450 2C19. The evidence suggests that Clomipramine may influence Cyp2c19 expression or activity, as it is linked to the development of anxiety states and abdominal disorders, both of which are associated with Cyp2c19 binding. This is further supported by the fact that Clomipramine and other related compounds, such as Imipramine and Felbamate, share a common pathway to Cyp2c19, indicating a potential role in modulating Cyp2c19 function. The presence of a common ancestor in the class of organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and tricyclic antidepressants suggests a broader pharmacological context, where these compounds may interact with Cyp2c19 through shared mechanisms. The integrated evidence points to a possible mechanism involving the regulation of Cyp2c19 by these compounds, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
